 cited thermodynamic-first QAOA theorem and the fixed-word moment theorem. No formalizes edge or kernel acceptance. This is a joint-disorder-and-measurement asymptotic statement, not a guarantee on every instance, a finite-size rate, a uniform p(n) claim, or an efficient angle-selection algorithm.","citation_ids":["qaoa_main_theorem","fggz2022_fixed_depth"],"evidence_ids":["concentration_source_warrant_pending"],"id":"circuit.one_measurement_near_optimum","kind":"claim","label":"One measured sample approaches the SK optimum with high joint probability","locator":"Derived in the long reasoning record, What is averaged, and a fixed-word probability consequence (#fixed-word-probability); premise locations are QAOA Theorem thm:main and FGGZ section 4 equations (13)–(14).","statement":"For every epsilon>0 there exist a finite depth p and fixed deterministic real angles, independent of n and the Gaussian disorder, such that Pr_{J,sigma}[H_n(sigma)/n >= P_star-epsilon] tends to 1 as n tends to infinity; sigma is one computational-basis measurement of the corresponding QAOA state.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.one_measurement_near_optimum","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.one_measurement_near_optimum","id":"field:fa2a27dafd4954120f3e5ca72d5022caaad16fc34615ea1710016d306d4680c5","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.one_measurement_near_optimum","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/assumptions.qaoa_model_and_limits"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.one_measurement_near_opti